From: kkw537 <171009921+kkw537@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: 200 ms awake after traffic in power save,
 not 2 s

In power save the driver uses PM_FAST: after a frame the radio stays
awake for pm2_sleep_ret milliseconds before it sleeps again.
brcmf_cfg80211_set_power_mgmt() sets that from cfg80211's timeout,
limited to 2000 ms with min_t(u32, ...). But cfg80211 passes -1 unless a
timeout was asked for, which only the wireless extensions can do
(nl80211 has no attribute for it), and -1 as a u32 is over the limit. So
every time power save is switched on, and every time the interface
comes up, the firmware is told to stay awake for two seconds after each
frame. With a frame every second or two (broadcasts, keepalives) the
radio then hardly sleeps while connected.

Use 200 ms when no timeout was asked for, and make it a parameter:

  /sys/module/brcmfmac/parameters/ps_timeout_ms

read whenever power save is set, so a new value takes effect the next
time the interface comes up or power save is switched. 2000 gives the
old behaviour back. A timeout that is asked for is passed on as before.

What it saves depends on the traffic and has not been measured. The
cost is latency: a reply that arrives more than 200 ms after the last
frame waits for the next beacon.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -88,6 +88,19 @@
 #define BRCMF_ND_INFO_TIMEOUT		msecs_to_jiffies(2000)
 
 #define BRCMF_PS_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS		2000
+#define BRCMF_PS_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS	200
+
+/*
+ * In power save, how long the radio stays awake after the last frame before
+ * it sleeps again (the firmware's pm2_sleep_ret), when cfg80211 asks for no
+ * particular time. Read whenever power save is set, so a change in
+ * /sys/module/brcmfmac/parameters/ps_timeout_ms takes effect the next time
+ * the interface comes up or power save is switched.
+ */
+static unsigned int brcmf_ps_timeout_ms = BRCMF_PS_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS;
+module_param_named(ps_timeout_ms, brcmf_ps_timeout_ms, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(ps_timeout_ms,
+		 "Time awake after traffic in power save (ms, up to 2000)");
 
 /* Dump obss definitions */
 #define ACS_MSRMNT_DELAY		80
@@ -3204,6 +3217,14 @@
 			bphy_err(drvr, "error (%d)\n", err);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * cfg80211 passes -1 unless a time was asked for (which only the
+	 * wireless extensions can do). As a u32 that was the maximum: two
+	 * seconds awake after every frame.
+	 */
+	if (timeout < 0)
+		timeout = brcmf_ps_timeout_ms;
+
 	err = brcmf_fil_iovar_int_set(ifp, "pm2_sleep_ret",
 				min_t(u32, timeout, BRCMF_PS_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS));
 	if (err)
